From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mining): reconcile completed and creative block breaks

Send MineBlock requests or legacy destroy transactions in PLAYER_AUTH_INPUT at the break tick, including the matching input flags. Predict damage for tagged vanilla tools and accept authoritative durability only for the same held stack. Handle creative start actions and suppress redundant mining swings; server correction remains authoritative for instant breaks.

Route creative breaks through Bedrock player actions while keeping survival completed-break inventory actions in the server-authoritative request. These paths share the block-breaking transaction and should be reviewed together.

Emit the completion Continue/Predict pair with its MineBlock request, then close the gesture with Abort in the following PLAYER_AUTH_INPUT frame. Paired protocol-2225 native controls separate these actions on every completed break, including rejected breaks and a tool change. Promote deferred actions after clearing the serialized frame so a subsequent Start follows the previous Abort. Actual cancellation and the legacy client-authoritative sequence retain their existing timing.

Keep a fresh survival Start pending until the completed gesture's Abort input has been serialized. Suppress continuation state while that Start is pending and cancel it on a real release. Native 1.26.60.5/protocol 2225 separates completion, Abort and restart across three inputs. Installed controls show that Java cooldowns alone move both input delivery and mining progress; own this boundary in the input-frame lifecycle instead. Regressions cover ordered promotion and release before promotion.

Retain direction changes while a Start waits for completion closure, without emitting Continue before that Start. The promoted action uses the latest direction.

